<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korean firms buy 50,000T corn, decline 52,500T.</title>
<headline>S.Korean firms buy 50,000T corn, decline 52,500T.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group of South Korean feed milling companies on Tuesday bought 50,000 tonnes of corn but passed on a tender for another 52,500 tonnes due to high prices, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the group included Cheiljedang Corp, Miwon Co Ltd, Woo Sung Feed Mill Co Ltd and Purina Korea Inc.</p>
